Interpretation
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* One server instance sustains ~5.89 files/min for this audio (46.88x real-time).
* Peak throughput 8.39 files/min at concurrency 2 = 1.42x over one job in flight (71% of linear).
* Below ~100% of linear, concurrent jobs are contending. The stage profile above localizes it: a stage whose mean grows in step with concurrency is serialized, one that stays flat is genuinely overlapping.
* Peak GPU memory ≈ 22369 MiB (+3744 MiB over idle at concurrency 1). Memory is rarely the binding constraint here; GPU compute is, so spreading replicas over --gpus buys more than stacking them on one.
* Quote a level's mean only alongside its sd/cv; with --repeat > 1 the across-repetitions table shows whether that mean is reproducible.

